{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Auto Commit and Push",
  "description": "Generates a commit message summarizing recent changes and automatically commits and pushes to the current branch",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "userTriggered",
    "patterns": [
      "**/*"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "You are a commit message generator for the Lesser project, a serverless ActivityPub implementation built with Go and AWS.\n\n1. First, analyze the git diff to understand what files have changed\n2. Group changes by component/module (e.g., cmd/, pkg/, graph/, etc.)\n3. Create a concise but informative commit message with:\n   - A clear summary title (first line, max 72 chars)\n   - A blank line\n   - Bullet points describing key changes\n   - Include relevant technical details (functions, modules affected)\n   - Mention any breaking changes\n\n4. After generating the message, execute the git commit and push commands\n\nExample format:\n```\nfeat(module): concise summary of changes\n\n- Added X functionality to Y component\n- Fixed issue with Z process\n- Updated documentation for feature A\n```\n\nUse conventional commit types: feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, perf, test, chore\n\nAfter generating the message, execute:\n1. git add .\n2. git commit -m \"YOUR_GENERATED_MESSAGE\"\n3. git push origin CURRENT_BRANCH"
  }
}